Tír na nÓg finds itself in Celtic legends as an otherworldly island existing beyond the western edges of the map that was home to the spirits. Known among Seekers as the phantom castle of Ireland, the fairies which inhabit the floating castle are the [[Titans]] known as [[Firbolg]] and [[Dullahan]]. {{Source|S2E48}}

[[Eathon Lambert]] took his wife, [[Sandra Lambert|Sandra]], on a moonlit picnic to the valley in [[County Kerry, Ireland]] to watch as Tír na nÓg appear in the moonlight. {{Source|S2E48}}

It was later found by [[Scarlet Byrne]], who was attacked by a rogue [[Firbolg]] Titan. Gaining the help of [[Lok Lambert]], who had been having recurring dreams of finding his father at such a place, she enlisted the help of the [[Huntik Foundation]] team to return. While exploring the castle, an area of the floor dematerialized, and Lok and [[Cherit]] fell into a weak point between dimensions. In this [[Inter-dimensional World]], he was able to speak to his father through a mirror into the [[Spirit World]], Huntik. After returning through the power of [[Umbra]], Lok invoked [[Pendragon]] to defeat the Dullahan and Firbolg Titans. Their [[Amulets]] secured, [[Den Fears]] bonded with one of the Dullahan Titans while Scarlet bonded with a Firbolg. {{Source|Back Home}}
